name: sim.writeCustomTableData
description: Deprecated. See properties instead
luaSynopsis: sim.writeCustomTableData(int objectHandle, string tagName, dict/list tableData)
pythonSynopsis: sim.writeCustomTableData(int objectHandle, string tagName, table tableData)
inputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the object where the data has to be stored, sim.handle_scene, sim.handle_app or sim.handle_appstorage
2. tagName: string that identifies the data. An empty string will remove all custom data
3. tableData: data to store. An empty array effectively removes the custom data from the object
outputs:
